From 2d431304f04b8ada48191e535004857f8074d13c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Lemar Gonzales <johnlemargonzales@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:36:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Open online chat and ElevenLabs voices to all signed-in
 accounts

- Chat (DeepSeek) and online speech now require an authenticated, active
  account instead of student_pro. Guests and disabled accounts stay denied;
  per-account quotas and usage recording are unchanged. Paid generation
  features (documents, flashcards, meeting notes) keep has_online_ai_access.
- New authenticated GET /v1/ai/tts/voices returns a bounded, cached,
  sanitized ElevenLabs catalogue ({provider, defaultVoiceId, voices}).
- POST /v1/ai/tts accepts an optional validated voiceId; explicit IDs must
  be in the current catalogue before any paid generation (unknown -> 422).
- Chat response adds provider and usedHandbook; the system prompt no longer
  claims the server saved local schedules.
- DEEPSEEK_MODEL defaults to deepseek-flash; the retired deepseek-v4-flash
  alias is normalized so existing deployments keep working.
